title: Aoi_Hangout1
---
Aoi: You again. Most people only come here at New Year.
Aoi: I'm writing up the lantern festival for the folklore club. Nobody else signed up, so I am the whole club.
-> What's so special about the lanterns?
    Aoi: They light them from the gate inward, one each night of the festival. The order never changes.
    Aoi: Old Mr. Kuroda says if you light them in the wrong order, winter comes early.
-> Can I help?
    Aoi: You can hold the notebook. That's a start.
-> Ever had a dream that felt too real? #needs:guts>=1
    Aoi: ...Snow. I dream about snow. In July. Don't laugh.
    <<flag aoi_snow_dream>>
Aoi: Come back sometime. The shrine is quieter than it looks.
===
title: Aoi_Hangout2
---
Aoi: There's a stone behind the main hall. Moss on the front, carving on the back.
Aoi: I made a rubbing. The script is old, but I've worked out most of the signs.
-> Show me.
    Aoi: This mark is "gate". This one is "cold". This one... I'm still not sure. Maybe "sleep".
-> Is it about the festival?
    Aoi: Partly. It reads like instructions. For what, I don't know yet.
Aoi: Here. I copied my notes for you. You look like someone who will need them.
<<give aoi_notes>>
You fold Aoi's notes on the old script into your pocket.
===
title: Aoi_Hangout3
---
Aoi: Can I tell you something odd? My grandmother lived by this shrine.
Aoi: She said that some summers, a few people in the neighbourhood wake at three and see snow.
Aoi: She said they always come back. Mostly.
-> I've seen it.
    Aoi: I know. You have the same look she had. Like you're cold in the middle of July.
    <<flag aoi_knows>>
-> That's just a story.
    Aoi: Maybe. Stories are how this town remembers things.
Aoi: Whatever it is, you're not the only one. Remember that.
===
title: Aoi_HangoutAgain
---
Aoi: Back again? Sit. The cicadas are loud today.
You talk about nothing much until the shadows grow long.
===
